1
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,360
I think your old classmate, Du Qingbo,

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,180
has ulterior motives.

3
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,080
That guy

4
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,300
is up to no good.

5
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:22,380
He wants to start with your mother

6
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:23,820
to exploit your weakness.

7
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:24,740
Yes.

8
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:27,540
That's what I'm worried about too.

9
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:30,340
My mom has always treated him like a son.

10
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:32,260
I'm just afraid of what he'll say to her

11
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:33,400
and worry her.

12
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,660
That's why you need to
communicate more with her.

13
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:38,140
First of all,

14
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:39,160
you have to find out

15
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,060
what Du Qingbo told her.

16
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:42,240
Second,

17
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:43,720
you need to let your mother know

18
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,420
your stance regarding Du Qingbo.

19
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:50,300
So talk to her more often.

20
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:53,900
Geng Qing, for those of us
in discipline inspection,

21
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:57,100
we always know exactly what to say
to our interviewees,

22
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:58,980
with endless patience
from God knows where.

23
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:00,420
But when we talk to our families,

24
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:01,740
we have no patience at all.

25
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:03,920
Geng Qing,

26
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:07,100
I know you've always wanted to be

27
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:08,820
a good man like your father.

28
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:10,460
In my eyes,

29
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,420
your father was a hero,

30
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,580
and you're a fine young man too.

31
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,380
Just go ahead and do your work boldly.

32
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:18,180
I'll back you up no matter what happens.

33
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,320
Hurry home and spend time with your mom.

34
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:24,100
Report to me as soon as anything comes up.

35
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:24,980
Okay.

36
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:25,580
Thank you, Secretary.

37
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:26,620
I'll take my leave.

38
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:27,940
Wait.

39
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:33,060
That blind date with Lin Lan last time...

40
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,620
Why didn't you go?

41
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:37,180
You even know about that?

42
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:40,460
Who in our office doesn't?

43
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,320
Everyone cares about you.

44
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:44,300
Fine, fine, forget it.

45
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,840
We can't meddle in you young people's affairs.

46
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,680
Back when my son was dating,

47
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,140
he never listened to me either.

48
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:52,620
Go on home.

49
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:55,240
All right.

50
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,520
Goodbye, Secretary.

51
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,280
Mom.

52
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:07,700
You're back, Qing.

53
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:09,120
Dinner will be ready soon.

54
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,820
Where did the stuff on the table come from?

55
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,480
Your Aunt Qin brought it over.

56
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,140
She's my old friend who was

57
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,000
a sent-down youth with me in the countryside.

58
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:31,900
Why would she give you such expensive gifts out of nowhere?

59
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:34,780
She wants to ask you for a favor, son.

60
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,600
They even promised

61
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,200
that if you agree to help,

62
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,100
they'd pull some strings later

63
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:47,100
to get you transferred to
a job in the province.

64
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:50,780
Qing!

65
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,280
Where are you going?

66
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:55,380
Come back.

67
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:00,620
Eat your dinner.

68
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,900
The head beneath an official's hat

69
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,480
must always remember who we are,

70
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:07,320
where we come from,

71
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:08,760
and who we serve.

72
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:10,160
Everyone,

73
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:11,580
did you hear that?

74
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:12,540
Mom,

75
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:14,180
the food you cooked

76
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,340
is really delicious.

77
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:17,040
Son,

78
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:19,280
what favor did Aunt Qin ask you to do?

79
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:20,920
Didn't she tell you?

80
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:22,860
She said you already know.

81
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,240
I don't.

82
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,200
How could you not know?

83
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:28,620
Lately,

84
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:29,940
you don't tell your mom anything.

85
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,080
Mom,

86
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:34,920
how many times have I told you?

87
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:36,920
When it comes to my work,

88
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,240
could you please stay out of it?

89
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:40,520
Geng Qing!

90
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:42,280
Mom,

91
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,600
I know you're close with Aunt Qin,

92
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,980
and she watched me grow up.

93
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,340
But if you accept gifts from her,

94
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,960
it's no different than me accepting them.

95
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,260
We have strict discipline rules.

96
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:54,220
Please don't push me to break them.

97
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,320
What kind of person do you take your mother for?

98
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,160
What are our family values?

99
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:00,840
Do you remember when you were little,

100
00:04:00,940 --> 00:04:03,240
you often listened to the opera
Fifteen Strings of Cash with Grandpa?

101
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:05,880
I was listening, too.

102
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:09,040
Prefect Kuang was upright and incorruptible.

103
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:12,860
He braved pressure from above
to retry those wrongful cases.

104
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:14,440
He wasn't afraid of offending people.

105
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:16,360
Now that's a true official.

106
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:19,640
An official who stands up for the common people!

107
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:22,240
When someone tries to win you over with favors,

108
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:24,440
you can't yield an inch.

109
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:26,500
Just do your duties honestly

110
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,360
and live with a clear conscience.

111
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:30,380
Mom,

112
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:32,700
does that mean

113
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,600
I should help Aunt Qin or not?

114
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,120
You've completely confused me.

115
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:41,080
Qing, do you really think I'm losing my mind?

116
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:44,480
Would I just watch my son go down the wrong path?

117
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:45,720
As for Aunt Qin,

118
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,360
I'll go explain things to her myself.

119
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:50,160
You just follow your conscience.

120
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,200
Mom,

121
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:55,360
thank you.

122
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:57,720
Eat, eat.

123
00:04:58,140 --> 00:04:59,560
After dinner,

124
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,820
take those gifts back to Aunt Qin.

125
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:04,080
How can an old lady like me carry all that?

126
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:06,680
Eat up.

127
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:08,800
I thought just now

128
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,240
you were really mad at me.

129
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:11,560
How could I be?

130
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:24,120
Hello?

131
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,540
Director Geng, can you come to the hospital?

132
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,160
Right now?

133
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:29,240
What is it?

134
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:30,940
A coworker gave me a ledger.

135
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:32,960
It seems to be for the Jianzhou Tunnel.

136
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:34,440
I feel like something bad is going to happen.

137
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:36,600
This ledger really isn't safe with me.

138
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:37,980
All right, I'll be right over.

139
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:39,900
Mom, I...

140
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:40,980
Hurry and go.

141
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,800
I'll reheat your food when you get back.

142
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:55,580
This ledger

143
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,240
should be the key to cracking the case.

144
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:01,340
We've already had experts
examine the ledger,

145
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:02,540
and it's not a forgery.

146
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,420
But so many years have passed,

147
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:07,380
and many viable leads are gone.

148
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:10,280
To dig up useful information again,

149
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,400
we'll still need some time.

150
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:32,600
Young Master Qin,

151
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,380
what's going on with that ledger?

152
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,580
It was truly an accident.

153
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,580
The finance office was moving,

154
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:41,160
and the ledger for the
Jianzhou Tunnel project back then

155
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:42,760
got thrown out as trash by the cleaner.

156
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,640
Who could have thought

157
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:47,000
Yao Yang's fellow townsman would pick it up?

158
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,820
Now the ledger is with
the Discipline and Inspection Committee.

159
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,080
What are your plans?

160
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:53,880
I know that.

161
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,360
Nothing is ever too big a deal for you.

162
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,480
As long as you secure
the Lu'an Group project,

163
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:00,560
you'll be fine.

164
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:01,760
No problem.

165
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,660
What about that classmate of yours?

166
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:05,620
If you can't bring yourself
to deal with him,

167
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:06,680
I'll take care of him for you.

168
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:07,580
Young Master Qin...

169
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:08,660
Wait...

170
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,460
we had an agreement on this before.

171
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,140
If someone has to go after him,

172
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,640
it has to be me.

173
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:19,020
Then you'd better not go soft on him.

174
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:00,380
Yanyan's here!

175
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:02,360
Uncle Geng, you're back from work!

176
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:04,020
Did you come by yourself?

177
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:06,260
Yanyan, stop playing games now.

178
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:07,480
Dinner is ready.

179
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:08,380
Okay, just a moment.

180
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,280
Almost done.

181
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,360
Come on, let's eat.

182
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,560
Yanyan said...

183
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:14,460
...she missed Mom's cooking.

184
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:15,820
I was craving it too,

185
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:16,620
so we came right over.

186
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:20,540
You're always welcome.

187
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,800
Eat up, Yanyan.

188
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,880
This is your favorite.

189
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:26,660
Yanyan,

190
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,620
of these four dishes Grandma made,

191
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:29,860
which one do you like best?

192
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:32,960
Braised pork!

193
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:35,540
You're growing right now,

194
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:36,860
so you should eat more shrimp.

195
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:38,700
Shrimp is packed with protein.

196
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,320
I just love meat.

197
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:46,180
Alright, go ahead.

198
00:08:46,740 --> 00:08:48,640
Have a piece of braised pork, then.

199
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,560
Thank you.

200
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,280
Mom,

201
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,580
this dish tastes incredible.

202
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:58,920
If you opened a restaurant,

203
00:08:58,920 --> 00:08:59,700
I'd invest in it!

204
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:00,820
Well,

205
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:02,300
wouldn't that work me to death?

206
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:03,720
You wouldn't have to cook.

207
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,640
Just give us the recipes.

208
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:06,500
We'd hire chefs.

209
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,300
Alright, alright.

210
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:09,560
Eat up, everyone.

211
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:10,400
Qing,

212
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:10,820
here.

213
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:21,580
You like spicy food.

214
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,120
Let me take that.

215
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:35,200
It's fine.

216
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,880
You insisted on coming along just to throw out the trash.

217
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:40,620
Qing.

218
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:42,660
Let's take a walk.

219
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,940
Sure, let's walk.

220
00:09:50,180 --> 00:09:51,820
Mom's cooking was so delicious.

221
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:52,740
Look how stuffed I am.

222
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:56,300
By the way,

223
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,920
that nursing home we took Mom
to see last time,

224
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:01,280
it's really great.

225
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,220
Think it over again.

226
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:04,980
I'm still holding that spot for Mom.

227
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,280
My mom is used to living with me.

228
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:11,160
I've never even thought about
putting her in a home.

229
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:13,320
I just wanted to do my duty as a son.

230
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:15,000
You won't give me a chance at all.

231
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:20,100
We haven't walked together
like this in a long time.

232
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:22,080
Yeah.

233
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,080
You're always so busy.

234
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,360
You're a top official at the
Discipline and Inspection Committee,

235
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,880
how would I dare disturb you?

236
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:30,140
Then...

237
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,320
why did you come today?

238
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:43,660
Did your Discipline and
Inspection Committee...

239
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,080
get a ledger from Yao Yang?

240
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:48,700
Look,

241
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:51,060
could you help find a way around this?

242
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:01,920
This ledger,

243
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:02,760
it...

244
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:04,460
it implicates a lot of people.

245
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,600
Some of them are even...

246
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:08,300
In short,

247
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:09,900
once this ledger is exposed,

248
00:11:09,900 --> 00:11:11,040
the consequences will be grave.

249
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:16,700
Qingbo.

250
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:18,260
Listen to me.

251
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:20,180
Turn yourself in.

252
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,220
Old classmate,

253
00:11:24,580 --> 00:11:26,720
for the sake of our years of friendship,

254
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:27,540
help me this once.

255
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:28,340
All these years,

256
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:30,380
I've never troubled you with work matters.

257
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,900
I really have nowhere left to turn.

258
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:34,800
Please, please, I'm begging you.

259
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,540
You aren't just facing me alone.

260
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,720
You are facing the Party and the people.

261
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:39,560
You know what?

262
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,720
If you don't help me this time,

263
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:45,340
you won't just be facing me alone, either.
